"""conf/code/dmimo.py -- SITE-SPECIFIC ray-traced testbed: DeepMIMO v4, 6 city scenarios at 28 GHz, prior id 'DMC'.

User decision 2026-10-10 CDT (conf/DECISIONS.md): run the receiver BLER on DeepMIMO -- the phase-0 "6 cities, block split"
configuration (conf/results/review_next/testbed2_phase0/report_deepmimo.md), with the channels generated by DeepMIMO's own
generator and at the SAME sizes as every other testbed (cell C2 = 8 x 4, N' = 1.6e5, GMM validation 5000, n = 2560 per SNR).
It runs through the D2 pipeline as a prior VARIANT of testbed D2 (TBID 2), like D3 / SV8e / MIX3 / UMi28: its own PID (11), so
every DMC stream is a NEW stream, and 'DMC' is in every output name (rung D2SXDMC<N>, ckpt d2sx_DMC_*, fits fit_DMC_Nr*_*,
sigma grid sigma_grid_D2_DMC).  common.make_gen / make_pilots dispatch here for prior in C.DM_PRIORS; every other path is
untouched.

Channel pool [built ONCE by conf/code/dmimo_build.py -- every choice is stated there; summary]
    ~/data/deepmimo/dmc_Nr<Nr>/H.npy   (pairs, Nr, Nt) complex64, uplink, H[a, b] = BS antenna a, UE antenna b
    DeepMIMO v4.0.5 dataset.compute_channels: BS Nr x 1 isotropic half-wavelength ULA with its boresight toward the centroid of
    its users, UE 4 x 1 ULA with a yaw ~ U[-180, 180) deg frozen per pair, 25 paths, narrowband at the carrier (subcarrier 0),
    per-pair path powers normalised to sum 1; pairs = every (scenario, BS, grid user) with a path.
    The files are NOT in git: POOL_SHA pins H.npy and split.npy, and a pool whose sha differs is refused.
This is a FIXED finite pool, not a generative model: a draw is an index into the pool.
Block split [frozen in split.npy]: 20 m position tiles; TEST tiles hold >= 15 % of the pairs; the pairs of the other tiles are
    the fit pool, except a frozen random 20000 = the validation pool.  Streams map onto the pools by their SEED LAYOUT
    (common.train_rng / trial_rng; the generator API carries no stream id, so it is read from rng.bit_generator.seed_seq):
        train stream 7  -> fit pool,  n DISTINCT pairs  (permutation; the equal-budget set N' = 160000 <= pool)
        train stream 8  -> validation pool, n distinct pairs (GMM validation; same tiles as the fit pool, disjoint pairs)
        train stream 10 -> TEST pool, i.i.d. with replacement (held-out reporting / GB')
        trial streams   -> TEST pool, i.i.d. with replacement (one index per trial)
        sparse_tune.py's development stream [20260930, TBID, PID, Nr, snr + 100] -> TEST pool, i.i.d. with replacement
            (added 2026-10-10 CDT for the baseline extension, after the DMC16e4 freeze and before any DMC BLER: baseline
            hyper-parameters are tuned on test-pool channels, like ALD's development TRIALS 2560.. of the trial stream --
            the same footing as every other dataset, whose development draws come from the test generator; it favours
            the baselines, never V1 / b*.  No existing stream changes.)
    Any other seed layout raises: a draw must never fall on the wrong side of the split silently.
    sample(rng) == sample_vecs(rng, 1)[0] (as a matrix) on every test stream.
Norm : ENSEMBLE normalisation E||H||_F^2 = Nr Nt: H = H_pool / sqrt(P_RAW), P_RAW = mean ||H_pool||_F^2 / (Nr Nt) over the
    train stream 7 (n = N_CAL = 160000), measured once by `python dmimo.py calibrate` and frozen below (the mix3.py pattern).
    Per-pair power keeps the multipath-interference variation.  vec is COLUMN-MAJOR, h[a + Nr b] = H[a, b]; complex128.
Pilot decision: the D2 T2b rule of common.make_pilots on Rt = E[H^H H] / Nr, estimated on the same N_CAL training channels and
    frozen below.  Constants exist for Nr = 8 x Nt = 4 only; another array raises (it needs its own build + calibrate + decision).
The testbed is FROZEN by the user decision: change nothing here without a new decision and a new prior id.
Second pool, prior 'SRT' (user instruction 2026-10-10 CDT: "Sionna에서도 진행하자"): Sionna RT 2.1 ray tracing, built ONCE by
    conf/code/srt_build.py (every choice is stated there) into ~/data/sionna_rt/srt_Nr<Nr>/{H.npy, split.npy}: the same file
    format, the same 20 m block split, the same stream -> pool mapping, calibration and pilot rule as DMC; its own PID (12),
    its own pinned sha and frozen constants below.  Nothing of DMC changes (`python dmimo.py selfcheck 8 DMC`).
"""
